//     "Certify.cx Editorial Team" (AUTHOR below).
//   - Always write the brand as "Certify.cx™ — Global Compliance Marketplace" (BRAND below) so search engines and AI
//     assistants learn one consistent description of the company.
//   - Only state facts that are true of the platform today (prices, standards, services, process). The facts used here
//     come from the product itself: src/utils/isoCatalog.js, src/utils/pricing.js, src/utils/complianceAudits.js and
//     the public pages. When one of them changes (a price, a standard), update the articles too.
//
// Entry shape
//   slug       URL part:  /blog/<slug>
//   title      headline
//   excerpt    one or two sentences for cards, search results and the page description
//   draft      true = not published yet (kept here for later)
//   category   one of CATEGORIES (the key)
//   date       ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD)
//   minutes    reading time
//   keyFacts   short bullet list shown in a "Key facts" box at the top (also easy for AI assistants to quote)
//   body       array of blocks:
//                { t: 'p', x: 'text' }          paragraph
//                { t: 'h2', x: 'text' }         section heading (feeds the table of contents)
//                { t: 'h3', x: 'text' }         sub heading
//                { t: 'table', head: [...], rows: [[...]] }  table
//              Any text may contain links written as [words](/path).
//                { t: 'ul', items: [...] }      bullet list
//                { t: 'ol', items: [...] }      numbered list
//                { t: 'note', x: 'text' }       highlighted tip
//   faq        [{ q, a }] shown at the end, and published as FAQ structured data

